error: 'scratch' does not live long enough

   ┌─ test/fail/11_store_child_arena.nul:15:15
   │
11 │     var scratch = arena.child()
   │         ───────  'scratch' is created here, as a child of 'arena'
   ·
13 │     var b = arena.create(Box)
   │         ─  'b' lives in 'arena'
   ·
15 │     b.arena = scratch
   │     ───────   ^^^^^^^  this names an arena that dies first
   │     │
   │     this memory lives in 'arena'
   ·
17 │     return b
   │            ─  'b' escapes here, so it outlives 'scratch'
   │
   = note: an arena stored in a struct is reachable from it, so it has to outlive
           it. 'scratch' is a child of 'arena' and dies first, which would leave
           'b' holding a name for memory that is gone.
   = help: store an arena that outlives 'b'
             b.arena = arena
